{"study_accession":"PRJNA1256360","secondary_study_accession":"SRP581956","title":"Selective modulation of gene expression in activated normal human peripheral blood mononuclear cells by store-operated calcium entry blocker BTP2","description":"Calcium is a critical signaling molecule in many cell types including immune cells. The calcium-release activated calcium channels (CRAC) responsible for store-operated calcium entry (SOCE) in immune cells are gated by STIM family members functioning as sensors of Ca2+ store content in the endoplasmic reticulum. We investigated the effect of SOCE blockers BTP2 and CM4620 on human peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) polyclonally-stimulated with the mitogen phytohemagglutinin (PHA). Overall design: To investigate the effect of SOCE blocker BTP2 on human peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) stimulated with the mitogen phytohemagglutinin (PHA), we performed bulk RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) and multiplexed single-cell RNA sequencing to query gene expression at the whole transcriptome level in human PBMCs from four healthy donors.","pubmed":"40654653","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN48188456","study_accession":"PRJNA1256360","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"bulkRNAseq_Donor4_PBMC+PHA+CM4620","description":"bulkRNAseq_Donor4_PBMC+PHA+CM4620","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8957667","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-05-04","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","PBMCs"],["treatment","PHA+CM4620"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33364218","experiment_accession":"SRX28608212","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":60918745,"base_count":12305586490,"first_public":"2025-05-04","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8957667: bulkRNAseq_Donor4_PBMC+PHA+CM4620 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"lab